1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,020
In 1902, a city started paying

2
00:00:02,020 --> 00:00:03,564
people for rat tails.

3
00:00:03,564 --> 00:00:04,741
Just the tails.

4
00:00:04,741 --> 00:00:07,899
Hanoi, French colonial Vietnam.

5
00:00:07,899 --> 00:00:09,884
The French built shiny new sewers

6
00:00:09,884 --> 00:00:11,034
under their quarter.

7
00:00:11,034 --> 00:00:12,508
Rats loved them.

8
00:00:12,508 --> 00:00:13,995
They climbed out of toilets,

9
00:00:13,995 --> 00:00:16,027
and plague was spreading across Asia.

10
00:00:16,027 --> 00:00:17,687
So the city made an offer:

11
00:00:17,687 --> 00:00:21,050
reportedly 1 cent for every rat tail.

12
00:00:21,050 --> 00:00:22,199
It worked.

13
00:00:22,199 --> 00:00:24,429
At the peak, over 20,000 tails

14
00:00:24,429 --> 00:00:25,873
came in a single day.

15
00:00:25,873 --> 00:00:28,091
Then officials spotted something odd:

16
00:00:28,091 --> 00:00:29,936
rats running around with no tails.

17
00:00:29,936 --> 00:00:31,457
People cut off the tail,

18
00:00:31,457 --> 00:00:32,571
let the rat go,

19
00:00:32,571 --> 00:00:34,375
and let it breed more tails.

20
00:00:34,375 --> 00:00:35,490
Inspectors even found

21
00:00:35,490 --> 00:00:37,092
rat farms outside the city.

22
00:00:37,092 --> 00:00:37,800
The hunt failed,

23
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:39,078
and the plague came anyway.

24
00:00:39,078 --> 00:00:41,098
Not hunters. Money.

25
00:00:41,098 --> 00:00:43,443
Pay for tails, and you get tails,

26
00:00:43,443 --> 00:00:44,730
not fewer rats.
